@node The command line
@chapter The command line

@table @code
@item esploro [@var{folder}]
@var{folder} (by default the one you're in) in the Esploro window on
your workspace, or a new one there.
@item esploro --new [@var{folder}]
A new Esploro window.
@item esploro @var{file}
The file's folder, with @var{file} selected.
@item esploro --where [@var{path}@dots{}]
Which windows have @var{path} open, or every file that's open.
@item esploro reveal
The file behind the window you're in, selected in its folder.
@item esploro recipe list
@itemx esploro recipe last
@itemx esploro recipe save @var{name}
@itemx esploro recipe forget @var{name}
@itemx esploro recipe run @var{name}|last @var{file}@dots{}
Recipes (@pxref{Recipes}): the last change, or one kept by name,
done again on @var{file}@dots{}.  A rename or a sorting goes to
Esploro for your review; with @option{--plan} (@code{run --plan}) it
only answers with the plan's file.
@item esploro recipe add @var{name} @var{recipe}
Keep @var{recipe}, an s-expression such as
@code{(:rename-by "IMG_*" "Pic #n")}, by name.
@item esploro rename-by [--plan] @var{from} @var{to} @var{file}@dots{}
@itemx esploro sort-by-kind [--plan] @var{file}@dots{}
Rename by a pattern, or sort into folders by kind
(@pxref{Recipes}): the plan goes to Esploro for your review.
@item esploro query [--lines] @var{words} [@var{folder}]
The files below @var{folder} that @var{words} describe
(@pxref{Searches}), one a line with @option{--lines}.
@item esploro search list
@itemx esploro search save @var{name} @var{words} [@var{folder}]
@itemx esploro search forget @var{name}
@itemx esploro search run [--lines] @var{name}
Searches kept by name.
@item esploro learn @var{proposed} @var{applied}
What @var{applied} (your plan) changed in @var{proposed} (an agent's),
as rules in words.
@item esploro learn --add @var{rule}
@var{rule} into @file{~/.config/esploro/sorting.md}, under its learnt
rules.
@item esploro habits [--new]
What you keep doing, each with a rule, a recipe and a search;
@option{--new}, only those not told of before.
@item esploro habits --dismiss @var{key}
That one, never offered again.
@item esploro archive open @var{path}
@itemx esploro archive close @var{mountpoint}
@itemx esploro archive list
An archive opened read-only like a folder (@pxref{Archives}), closed,
and the ones open.
@item esploro duplicates [--plan] @var{folder}
The files below @var{folder} that are the same, byte for byte, in
groups; @option{--plan}, the copies to the Trash as a plan to review.
@item esploro sizes [--lines] @var{folder}
Its entries by the space they take, biggest first.  With
@code{--lines}, for a shell or an agent: bytes, a tab and the whole
path, a line each.
@item esploro sizes --below [--lines] @var{folder}
The biggest things anywhere below it (Biggest Anywhere Below).
@item esploro sizes --trash
What the things in the Trash take, and how many there are.
@item esploro recent [--lines]
The files opened lately, newest first.
@item esploro workspaces
StumpWM's workspaces, each with the project its windows are about.
@item esploro open-on @var{n} @var{path}@dots{}
Goes to workspace @var{n} and opens @var{path} there.
@item esploro selection [--sexp]
The files selected in Esploro, or dired, used last, one a line;
@option{--sexp} gives @code{(:selection @var{folder} (@var{file}@dots{}))}.
@item esploro propose @var{file} [@var{why}]
A plan for you to review in Esploro (what an agent's proposal runs).
@item esploro --dbus
Makes the running Emacs answer @code{org.freedesktop.FileManager1},
the file manager's name on D-Bus that browsers call for ``Show in
folder''.  A D-Bus service file naming it starts it the first time
it's asked (Vikix puts one in @file{~/.local/share/dbus-1/services}).
@end table

What the window uses (each answers with one s-expression):

@table @code
@item esploro apply [@var{file}]
Applies the plan in @var{file}, or on standard input: one step a line,
@code{(:copy "/from" "/to")}, @code{(:move @dots{})},
@code{(:rename "/path" "new name")}, @code{(:mkdir "/path")},
@code{(:trash "/path")}.  Anything else is refused.
@item esploro undo
Undoes the last applied plan.
@item esploro where @var{folder}
The files in @var{folder} a window has open.
@item esploro open @var{path}
Goes to the window that has @var{path}, or opens it.
@item esploro project [@var{path}]
@var{path}'s project, and the windows that have something in it.
@item esploro focus @var{id}
Goes to the window @var{id} (StumpWM's).
@item esploro thumbnails [--size @var{n}] @var{path}@dots{}
Small PNGs of pictures, PDFs and videos for the list, each made once.
@item esploro preview @var{path}
A PNG of @var{path} (a picture, a PDF or a video), made once and kept.
@item esploro trash-list
@itemx esploro restore @var{name}@dots{}
@itemx esploro empty-trash
The Trash.
@end table

@node Writing commands
@chapter Writing commands

Commands are on Esploro's menus (File @result{} Commands, and the
right-click menu), and anywhere in Emacs on a file name: with embark,
@kbd{C-.} then @kbd{,} (comma) offers Esploro's commands for the file (in a
minibuffer, dired, or at point), and @kbd{J} shows it in Esploro.
@kbd{M-x esploro-file-commands} asks for a file.  For that before Esploro
is first opened, your Emacs loads its little loader at the start:

@lisp
(load "~/.local/opt/esploro/emacs/esploro-loaddefs" t t)
@end lisp

On Vikix, @kbd{Super+Alt+x} offers them for the file behind any window,
in rofi.


The core defines commands once, for the kinds of file they're for:

@lisp
(esploro:define-file-command shrink ((path :image) :changes t)
  "Plan a smaller copy beside it."
  (list (list :copy path (esploro::free-name path " small"))))
@end lisp

Kinds: @code{:folder}, @code{:image}, @code{:video}, @code{:audio},
@code{:pdf}, @code{:text}, @code{:lisp}, @code{:archive}, @code{:file}
(anything but a folder) and @code{t} (anything).  A command with
@code{:changes t} returns plan steps instead of touching files, so it
is checked, journaled and undoable like the rest.  Offering these in
the window's menus is the next step.

@bye
